label: Fetch Rate
description: >-
  Ask the upstream service for a rate. The only node in the example corpus that
  declares an `effect:`, and the only one whose output is not guaranteed by the
  acceptance gate — a host handler never passes through it.

  So this node's output is asserted at RUNTIME, against `Rate`, before it can
  reach the log. That is not a special case for effects; it is where the
  equivalent of the gate has to live for code the gate never saw. If the
  handler returns a string where `rate` should be a number, or omits
  `provenance`, or invents a `provenance` outside the declared enum, the result
  never becomes a Rate: it becomes `Failed_RateRequest`, carrying the original
  request and the reason.

  `examples/flaky-source/effects.ts` misbehaves ON PURPOSE. That is the point
  of the example.
effect: http
input: RateRequest
output: Rate
